To install waydroid on steam frame you have to do several things:

A) install dependencies that waydroid needs, but don't install over packages that already exist on SteamOS natively.
B) install the ARM64 version of waydroid
C) Take into account when to make steamos readonly and when not
D) Also make sure to not install waydroid directly into /var as there is not enough space, you have to map it to another location with symlinks
E) Once waydroid is installed you need to open up the firewall
	sudo -S firewall-cmd --zone=trusted --add-interface=waydroid0 &>
  sudo -S firewall-cmd --zone=trusted --add-port=53/udp
	sudo -S firewall-cmd --zone=trusted --add-port=67/udp
	sudo -S firewall-cmd --zone=trusted --add-forward
	sudo -S firewall-cmd --runtime-to-permanent
F) You may need to start FAKEWIFI
waydroid prop set persist.waydroid.fake_wifi "*"

Notes:
Useful Commands
waydroid session start
waydroid session stop
waydroid show-full-ui
systemctl restart waydroid-container

Getting Android ID for Play Store Activation:
sudo waydroid shell -- sh -c "sqlite3 /data/data/*/*/gservices.db 'select value from main where name = \"android_id\";'"
